Engine derivation
description: memberships are ordinary graph edges - the engine derives the views
- >
  Fragments and memberships are ordinary graph data, so the engine derives the views:
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: bullets>
  - '**A node''s ontos** = its membership edges walked UP: `: N: ?..: !!<format: x-yamlover-onto>` - every parent of N (bookmark-created ones included) that is an onto; a fragment''s ontos likewise from the fragment member.'
  - '**Materials filed under an onto** (`/api/tagged`) = the onto''s own keyless members: `O: -` - each surfacing as its owning material, or as a fragment of it.'
  - '**Highlighting** reads the member fragment''s selector (and its `image` crop) for the region.'
